From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: howeasy <howardabudd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:36:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] slink: Polished Crystal variant forms in the pool

Owner ruling 2026-10-04: a regional/variant form is a different Pokemon
from its species, a cosmetic form is the same one. getPokemon() now holds
every BaseData record, the 46 variant forms (records 292..337) included,
so wild, trainer, starter, static and trade pools draw them with their
own stats and types; UPR alt-forme options stay off. EGG, the unused $100
and Unown stay banned.

A site reads as the record its (species, form) resolves to (variant form,
else the species), so formed wild slots, trainer mons, script sites and
trade sides join the model. writeSpecies is the one writer: a site that
still holds the same record is untouched (a cosmetic form stays);
otherwise LOW(species), then the site gender/egg bits, HIGH(species) << 5
and the variant form, the site own NO_FORM/PLAIN_FORM, or the context
plain spelling. The ini supplement adds the five resolved formed script
sites as StaticSite44..48.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
